## Comparison

| $a$ | $X_a$ | Digits |
|-----|-------|--------|
| 1 | 1222222221 | 10 |
| 2 | 333333 | 6 |
| 3 | 333333 | 6 |
| 4 | **4455** | **4** |
| 5 | 666666 | 6 |
| 6 | 666666 | 6 |
| 7 | 7777777788 | 10 |

The smallest value is $\boxed{4455}$, arising from clearance level $a=4$. It is a 4-digit number (all others have 6 or 10 digits), composed of digits 4 and 5, with digit sum $4+4+5+5=18\equiv 0\pmod{9}$ and alternating sum $4-4+5-5=0\equiv 0\pmod{11}$, hence divisible by $99$: $4455 = 45 \times 99$.

